IMPORT `pti268-definitions`
IMPORT `pti268-extensions`

-- Part IV, general exclusions (IV. NHỮNG ĐIỂM LOẠI TRỪ), lines 587-680 of the source.
-- The chapeau excludes costs relating to death, injury or illness caused by any of the
-- circumstances listed, for every benefit and every extension clause:
-- src:587 | IV. NHỮNG ĐIỂM LOẠI TRỪ
-- src:588 | A. CÁC LOẠI TRỪ CHUNG ÁP DỤNG CHO CÁC ĐIỀU KIỆN BẢO HIỂM
-- src:589 | (BAO GỒM CẢ CÁC ĐIỀU KHOẢN MỞ RỘNG)
-- src:590 | Các chi phí phát sinh liên quan đến tử vong hoặc thương tật, bệnh tật xảy ra bởi các
-- src:591 | trường hợp sau đây sẽ không được bảo hiểm:
--
-- HOW THIS IS ENCODED. Each circumstance in pti268-nouns.l4 is a fact; the rule below maps
-- each one to the numbered exclusion it engages, or to NOTHING where the text carves it
-- out. Three exclusions turn on dates or on the treatment rather than on a listed fact and
-- are derived: 5 (treatment without a doctor's indication), 13 (indicated or injured before
-- the start date), and the second 32 (special or pre-existing disease in the first year).
--
-- Fork F14: where an exclusion admits a narrower and a wider reading, the narrower is
-- taken, as Law 08/2022/QH15 art 24 directs for an unclear term (LAW: law-08-2022-qh15.txt
-- line 588-591). Each such choice is named where it is made.

§ `Part IV — General exclusions`

§§ `The insured's age at the event`

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the insured's age at the event in` claim MEANS
    `age in completed years of a person born on` (claim's `the insured person`'s `date of birth`) `on` (claim's `the event`'s `date`)

§§ `Exclusions 1 to 32: the listed circumstances`

