-- Notes on particular items, each a fork recorded in NOTES.md:
-- * 2: a traffic offence is excluded only from age 14 (F16): a younger insured's traffic
--   offence is not caught by the general "breach of the law" limb either, or the age limit
--   would be empty.
-- * 5: the vaccination limb spares the "newborn care benefit", which Part II never grants
--   (finding X7); the near miss is kept so a case can say it falls there.
-- * 8: a strike is not excluded where the contract carries VI.5 (F29).
-- * 16: a routine prenatal check is not excluded where VI.12 covers it.
-- * 23: does not apply to Benefit 2.
-- * 28: "Tham gia tập luyện hoặc tham gia thi đấu" (training or competing) governs all three
--   objects, so a dangerous sport or a race taken up for leisure, outside training and
--   competition, is not caught (F15, the narrower reading); "any race" includes the charity
--   and company races def 62 spares (finding X9).
GIVEN c     IS A `A circumstance`
      claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A general exclusion`
`the general exclusion engaged by` c `in` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `an intentional act of the insured`                                          THEN JUST `exclusion 1`
    WHEN `an intentional act of the insured's lawful heir`                            THEN JUST `exclusion 1`
    WHEN `a breach by the insured of the law, or of rules of a local authority or a lawful body` THEN JUST `exclusion 2`
    WHEN `a breach of traffic law by the insured`                                     THEN
        IF `the insured's age at the event in` claim AT LEAST 14 THEN JUST `exclusion 2` ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `the insured under the influence of alcohol or beer above the legal limit`   THEN JUST `exclusion 3`
    WHEN `the insured under the influence of another stimulant`                       THEN JUST `exclusion 3`
    WHEN `the insured having drunk alcohol within the legal limit`                    THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a fight the insured took part in`                                           THEN JUST `exclusion 4`
    WHEN `a fight the insured took part in, proven to be only in self-defence`        THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `treatment or medicine without a doctor's indication and prescription`       THEN JUST `exclusion 5`
    WHEN `treatment not recognised by science, or experimental`                       THEN JUST `exclusion 5`
    WHEN `a vaccination`                                                              THEN JUST `exclusion 5`
    WHEN `a vaccination needed after an accident or an insect or animal bite`         THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a vaccination under the newborn care benefit`                               THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `preventive medicine`                                                        THEN JUST `exclusion 5`
    WHEN `functional food`                                                            THEN JUST `exclusion 5`
    WHEN `aviation other than as a ticketed passenger`                                THEN JUST `exclusion 6`
    WHEN `air travel as a ticketed passenger`                                         THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `military training exercises`                                                THEN JUST `exclusion 6`
    WHEN `combat with the armed forces`                                               THEN JUST `exclusion 6`
    WHEN `an earthquake`                                                              THEN JUST `exclusion 7`
    WHEN `a volcanic eruption`                                                        THEN JUST `exclusion 7`
    WHEN `radioactive contamination`                                                  THEN JUST `exclusion 7`
    WHEN `war`                                                                        THEN JUST `exclusion 8`
    WHEN `civil war`                                                                  THEN JUST `exclusion 8`
    WHEN `a strike`                                                                   THEN
        IF `VI.5 lifts the strike exclusion under` (claim's `the contract`) THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `exclusion 8`
    WHEN `terrorism`                                                                  THEN JUST `exclusion 8`
    WHEN `a riot or civil commotion`                                                  THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `syphilis`                                                                   THEN JUST `exclusion 9`
    WHEN `gonorrhoea`                                                                 THEN JUST `exclusion 9`
    WHEN `pulmonary tuberculosis`                                                     THEN JUST `exclusion 9`
    WHEN `malaria`                                                                    THEN JUST `exclusion 9`
    WHEN `leprosy`                                                                    THEN JUST `exclusion 9`
    WHEN `treatment of a sexually transmitted disease`                                THEN JUST `exclusion 10`
    WHEN `an illness related to HIV or AIDS`                                          THEN JUST `exclusion 10`
    WHEN `treatment at home, other than by a home care nurse`                         THEN JUST `exclusion 11`
    WHEN `care by a home care nurse`                                                  THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `treatment at a hydrotherapy or natural-methods institute, a spa, a sanatorium or a similar place` THEN JUST `exclusion 11`
    WHEN `treatment of a mental illness`                                              THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `an acute mental disorder whose symptoms end once treatment stabilises it`   THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a psychological disorder`                                                   THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `memory impairment`                                                          THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `neurasthenia`                                                               THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `physical debility with no specific pathological cause`                     THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `fatigue`                                                                    THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `stress`                                                                     THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `a sleep disorder`                                                           THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `treatment of premenopause or menopause`                                     THEN JUST `exclusion 12`
    WHEN `treatment or surgery related to reproduction`                               THEN JUST `exclusion 14`
    WHEN `maternity care of a pregnancy by artificial insemination or in vitro fertilisation` THEN JUST `exclusion 15`
    WHEN `a periodic health check, or a check before travel or work`                  THEN JUST `exclusion 16`
    WHEN `a hospital stay or consultation only for a check, unrelated to treatment`   THEN JUST `exclusion 16`
    WHEN `a gynaecological or andrological examination to treat an illness`          THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a routine prenatal check`                                                   THEN
        IF `VI.12 covers routine prenatal checks under` (claim's `the contract`) THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `exclusion 16`
    WHEN `a routine eye or hearing test`                                              THEN JUST `exclusion 16`
    WHEN `surgery or treatment of a degenerative defect of hearing or sight`          THEN JUST `exclusion 16`
    WHEN `a refractive error of the eye`                                              THEN JUST `exclusion 16`
    WHEN `eye strain`                                                                 THEN JUST `exclusion 16`
    WHEN `surgery to restore sight`                                                   THEN JUST `exclusion 17`
    WHEN `cataract surgery for a pathological cause`                                  THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `treatment or surgery at the insured's request, not on a doctor's indication` THEN JUST `exclusion 18`
    WHEN `routine treatment as prescribed by the Ministry of Health`                 THEN JUST `exclusion 18`
    WHEN `orthopaedics or rehabilitation that does not follow treatment of an illness` THEN JUST `exclusion 19`
    WHEN `upkeep or repair of a prosthesis or an artificial device`                   THEN JUST `exclusion 20`
    WHEN `a dietary supplement available without prescription`                        THEN JUST `exclusion 21`
    WHEN `family planning`                                                            THEN JUST `exclusion 22`
    WHEN `infertility treatment`                                                      THEN JUST `exclusion 22`
    WHEN `purchase of a prosthesis that does not sustain life`                        THEN
        IF claim's `the benefit claimed` EQUALS `Benefit 2` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `exclusion 23`
    WHEN `cosmetic treatment or surgery`                                              THEN JUST `exclusion 24`
    WHEN `treatment at a doctor's private clinic outside office hours, with no financial invoice` THEN JUST `exclusion 25`
    WHEN `weight control treatment`                                                   THEN JUST `exclusion 26`
    WHEN `treatment or surgery of a congenital defect or disease, or a genetic malformation` THEN JUST `exclusion 27`
    WHEN `taking part in an activity` activity income training match                   THEN
        IF       (training OR match)
             AND (income OR `a dangerous sport` activity OR `a race` activity)
        THEN JUST `exclusion 28`
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `purchase, upkeep, fitting or repair of spectacles, crutches, a wheelchair, a hearing or sight aid or an orthopaedic device` THEN JUST `exclusion 29`
    WHEN `extraction of a milk tooth`                                                 THEN JUST `exclusion 30`
    WHEN `examinations and tests without a doctor's conclusion of illness`           THEN JUST `exclusion 31`
    WHEN `an epidemic declared by a competent authority`                              THEN JUST `exclusion 32`
    WHEN `asphyxiation caused by the insured's own intentional act`                   THEN JUST `exclusion 1`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Exclusion 5, as the treatment shows it`

-- Treatment without a doctor's indication and prescription is excluded whether or not the
-- claim lists it as a circumstance: a course of treatment not on the indication of someone
-- who counts as a doctor (def 1, def 17) engages exclusion 5.
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exclusion 5 is engaged by the treatment in` claim IF
    CONSIDER claim's `the outcome`
    WHEN `medical expenses` t items THEN NOT `on the indication of a doctor` t
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Exclusion 13: indicated, or injured, before the start date`

-- Surgery indicated before the start date, and costs of treating an injury from an
-- accident that happened before the start date; not applied where the contract extends to
-- pre-existing conditions. The start date is def 38's (fork F1).
-- src:621 | 13. Những chỉ định phẫu thuật có từ trước ngày bắt đầu bảo hiểm, chi phí y tế để điều trị
-- src:622 | thương tật do tai nạn đã xảy ra trước ngày bắt đầu bảo hiểm (không áp dụng đối với các hợp
-- src:623 | đồng mở rộng bảo hiểm cho tình trạng có sẵn);
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exclusion 13 is engaged by` claim IF
        NOT claim's `the contract`'s `cover for pre-existing conditions agreed in writing`
    AND (   `indicated before the start date`
         OR (    `counts as an accident under` (claim's `the contract`) (claim's `the event`)
             AND claim's `the event`'s `date` LESS THAN `the start date`))
    WHERE
        `the start date` MEANS `the start date for` (claim's `the insured person`)
        `indicated before the start date` MEANS
            CONSIDER claim's `the event`'s `date surgery was first indicated`
            WHEN JUST d  THEN d LESS THAN `the start date`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `The second exclusion 32: special or pre-existing disease in the first year`

-- A special disease, or a pre-existing one, in the first policy year, for Benefit 4
-- (hospital and surgery) and Benefit 6 (outpatient), as the table says by the size of the
-- group (persons insured) and the person's place in it:
-- src:674 | 32. Bệnh đặc biệt, hoặc bệnh có sẵn trong năm bảo hiểm đầu tiên. Loại trừ này sẽ áp dụng
-- src:675 | cho điều kiện 4 (Nằm viện phẫu thuật do bệnh & thai sản) và 6 (điều trị ngoại trú) như sau:
-- src:678 | Số người bảo hiểm trong một nhóm Nhân viên Người thân trong gia đình
-- src:679 | - Nhóm từ 30 người trở lên 6 tháng 1 năm
-- src:680 | - Nhóm trên 50 người Không 6 tháng
-- The table is generated into `the months the second exclusion 32 runs for` below; its
-- figures are "6 tháng", "1 năm", "Không" (none) and "6 tháng".
-- Forks: F12 (a group under 30, which the table omits, falls under the sentence's own
-- "first policy year", 12 months); F33 (a group of more than 50 is also "30 or more": the
-- row for "trên 50" governs, since otherwise it would never apply); F11 (for Benefits 4 and
-- 6 this table, not III.8's 365 days, measures the wait for special and pre-existing
-- disease in a group of 30 or more; see pti268-conditions.l4 and finding X3).
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months the second exclusion 32 runs for` claim MEANS
    --                                                    employee  family
    BRANCH IF `the group` GREATER THAN 50 THEN IF `an employee` THEN 0 ELSE 6
           IF `the group` AT LEAST 30     THEN IF `an employee` THEN 6 ELSE 12
           OTHERWISE                           12
    WHERE
        `the group`   MEANS claim's `the contract`'s `persons insured in the group`
        `an employee` MEANS claim's `the insured person`'s `role` EQUALS `an employee`

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special or pre-existing disease in` claim IF
        `a special disease` (claim's `the event`'s `diagnosis`)
    OR  `a pre-existing condition, judged at` (`the start date for` (claim's `the insured person`)) `for` (claim's `the event`)

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the second exclusion 32 is engaged by` claim IF
        (   claim's `the benefit claimed` EQUALS `Benefit 4`
         OR claim's `the benefit claimed` EQUALS `Benefit 6`)
    AND `a special or pre-existing disease in` claim
    AND claim's `date of the loss` LESS THAN
            `add months` (`the start date for` (claim's `the insured person`)) (`the months the second exclusion 32 runs for` claim)

§§ `All the general exclusions a claim engages`

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A general exclusion`
`the general exclusions engaged by` claim MEANS
    append (mapMaybe (GIVEN c YIELD `the general exclusion engaged by` c `in` claim) (claim's `the event`'s `circumstances`))
           (append `exclusion 5 by the treatment`
                   (append `exclusion 13` `the second 32`))
    WHERE
        `exclusion 5 by the treatment` MEANS
            IF `exclusion 5 is engaged by the treatment in` claim THEN LIST `exclusion 5` ELSE EMPTY
        `exclusion 13` MEANS
            IF `exclusion 13 is engaged by` claim THEN LIST `exclusion 13` ELSE EMPTY
        `the second 32` MEANS
            IF `the second exclusion 32 is engaged by` claim THEN LIST `the second exclusion 32` ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general exclusion applies to` claim IF
    NOT null (`the general exclusions engaged by` claim)
